<title>USA: Converse stake cut by Vinik group to 3.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Converse stake cut by Vinik group to 3.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by former Fidelity Magellan Fund manager Jeffrey Vinik said Monday it cut its stake in Converse Inc to 540,000 shares, or 3.1 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said it sold a net of more than 500,000 common shares in the Boston-based athletic footwear maker between March 25 and April 18 at $14.72 to $18.93 each.</p>
</text>
